			"Message": "perf(Element): Coalesce high-frequency IPC emits and restore webview rendering\n\nSynchronize 11 Element submodules to address IPC saturation during extension boot and fix webview initialization failures.\n\nMountain introduces batched emits for Decoration, Progress, and TreeView handlers, grouping high-frequency notifications (e.g., 6000+ git progress updates) into 16ms frames to prevent WKWebView channel starvation. Implement deduplication for filesystem watchers and single-flight directory walks to reduce kernel resource exhaustion. Standardize IPC variable names to PascalCase and fix URI normalization for workspace paths.\n\nSky adds a placeholder registry for webview creation to prevent silent drops of `set-html` calls before the workbench accessor is ready, and optimizes bridge logging to emit only on first resolution. Wind normalizes trailing slashes in workspace folder URIs to ensure correct relative path resolution for breadcrumbs.\n\nOutput restores eager paint overrides and re-enables `isolation: isolate` CSS to fix layout issues, while injecting the missing `IWebviewWorkbenchService` to render extension panels like Roo and Claude. Other submodules (Cocoon, Common, Echo, etc.) sync to include dependency updates (pnpm, wrangler) and maintain consistency.\n\nThese changes restore input responsiveness during heavy extension activation and ensure reliable rendering of complex extension features.",
			"SHA": "ffb68d18bd2e474842cbbdc8c1ae580b32b0ddcd"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-01T01:32:38Z",
			"File": [
				"⡟⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				4
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Element): Sync submodules with PascalCase naming convention\n\nSynchronize four Element submodules with PascalCase refactoring:\n- Air: Rename CLI handlers (handle_status → Status, handle_restart → Restart, handle_config → Config, handle_metrics → Metrics, handle_logs → Logs, handle_debug → Debug) and plugin trait methods (handle_message → Message, handle_event → Event)\n- Grove: Rename handle_call → Call in APIBridgeImpl\n- Mountain: Rename IPC handler functions (handle_commands_execute → CommandsExecute, handle_configuration_get → ConfigurationGet, handle_incoming_message →IncomingMessage, etc.)\n\nThese changes align with the project's naming convention specified in CLAUDE.md, removing handle_ prefixes for shorter, consistent method names across the codebase.\n\nAdditionally, Sky adds an event-driven installation path for Wind's LandWorkbench bridge that listens for cel:services-ready, ensuring proper sequencing: services DI container populated → install Wind bridge → notify subscribers.",
			"SHA": "e86cbf076d24ae8068136ca73697bf3d16e1ce3c"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-01T01:17:53Z",
			"File": [
				"⡟⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				4
			],
			"Message": "perf(Element): Batch command registration to eliminate IPC saturation during extension boot\n\nSynchronize four Element submodules with coordinated performance fixes addressing keystroke lag during extension boot:\n\n- Mountain (f304bd40): Add CommandEmitBatch to buffer 1000+ registerCommand notifications and flush after 16ms, reducing individual emit storms to single batched IPC round-trip\n- Output (2afe4b46): Revert DisableLazyPaint opt-in gate (regressed editor mount) and remove PartZIndexCSS `isolation: isolate` rule that blocked input events under WKWebView while keeping CSS lazy-paint fix\n- Sky (06fd1942): Accept batched `{ commands: [...] }` format alongside legacy single-command shape via new RegisterOneCommand helper\n- Cocoon: Sync to latest (a877808c)\n\nThese changes prevent 1000+ Tauri events per extension boot from saturating the shared WKWebView IPC channel that also delivers keystrokes, restoring input responsiveness during the most resource-intensive phase.",
			"SHA": "16654395ae34db87fbc5e301bdc94688e202a995"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-01T00:36:04Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Output): Make DisableLazyPaint RAF/IO overrides opt-in\n\nWrap the requestAnimationFrame and IntersectionObserver overrides in a conditional guard. These overrides redirect Monaco's rAF callbacks to the macrotask queue and replace native IntersectionObserver with a fire-on-observe stub that calls getBoundingClientRect() synchronously.\n\nThe problem: both bypass WKWebView's compositor-frame coordination—which also delivers keyboard input. Once Monaco starts rendering (theme load, decorations, cursor blink, minimap, scrollbars), the macrotask queue floods and keystrokes starve, causing the input lag symptom this polyfill was meant to solve.\n\nSolution: make these overrides opt-in via `__LAND_AGGRESSIVE_LAZY_PAINT__ = true` set BEFORE workbench bootstrap. Keep the CSS lazy-paint kill (content-visibility: visible) always applied—it solves the original \"panels invisible until hover/scroll\" WKWebView bug without affecting input latency.\n\nThis complements the recent IPC logging fix (2588fe4) and EditContext polyfill (44e160c) in addressing WKWebView input starvation.",
			"SHA": "7df7d851b9734f17560e6323145e1544c3962d05"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-01T00:16:11Z",
			"File": [
				"⡿⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				5
			],
			"Message": "perf(Element): Reduce IPC channel saturation to fix keystroke lag during extension boot\n\nSynchronize five Element submodules with performance optimizations addressing input lag caused by IPC channel saturation:\n- Mountain: Gate mountain_sync_status_update and mountain_performance_update events behind LAND_SYNC_STATUS_EMIT and LAND_PERF_EMIT env vars. Add subscriber fast-path to skip lock-and-drain when Subscribers.is_empty().\n- Output: Remove success-case tauri-invoke logging in InvokeMountain and fire-and-forget channel stub logging. Only log drift disposition (uncovered commands).\n- Sky: Remove per-fire _CelDispatchLog traces (now requires __LAND_TRACE_CEL_DISPATCH__=true). Diagnostic bridges for markers-bridge and webview-bridge now only log on pushable=false or hasRegister=false.\n- Wind: Remove success-case tauri-invoke forward (failures still forwarded). Remove fire-and-forget stub logging entirely. Only forward drift disposition case.\n\nThese changes prevent 50-100 log/emits per second during extension boot from saturating Tauri's invoke channel and starving keystroke delivery on the shared WebKit message channel.",
			"SHA": "2082615be7eab87db7b9a1b0931b9697d916fdb5"
		}
	],
